#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""HF band planning with VOACAP (voacapl), with no internet: how likely each band is
to get through from this station to a place, hour by hour (UTC), for a month.

  emcomm-voacap choices                  the places, modes, antennas, powers and noise
                                         levels a plan can use, as JSON
  emcomm-voacap targets                  the places, one JSON line each
  emcomm-voacap ssn [--month YYYY-MM]    the sunspot number used for a month, as JSON
  emcomm-voacap plan --to PLACE [--month YYYY-MM] [--ssn N] [--mode MODE]
                     [--antenna ANTENNA] [--power WATTS] [--noise NOISE]
                                         the prediction, as JSON

PLACE is a target's id (near:250, us:MA, dx:london...) or grid:FN42 for any grid
square. The station's own position is its grid square (Settings > User). Each
prediction runs VOACAP's point-to-point method 30 for the ten HF bands, 24 hours.

The sunspot number is the smoothed one VOACAP is built on: NOAA's monthly forecast
(the Online page saves it when the station is online) or, before that, a built-in
estimate of solar cycle 25's decline.
"""

